WEBVTT

00:12:27.559 --> 00:12:30.173
When you meet a new technology, stop,

00:12:30.197 --> 00:12:32.726
until it can be proven
that it does no harm."

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.995
I think that really leads nowhere.

00:12:35.019 --> 00:12:38.020
But a better way is
what I call the proactionary principle,

00:12:38.044 --> 00:12:40.450
which is, you engage with technology.

00:12:40.474 --> 00:12:41.852
You try it out.

00:12:41.876 --> 00:12:46.092
You obviously do what the precautionary
principle suggests,

00:12:46.116 --> 00:12:47.361
you try to anticipate it,

00:12:47.385 --> 00:12:48.812
but after anticipating it,

00:12:48.836 --> 00:12:50.351
you constantly asses it,

00:12:50.375 --> 00:12:51.938
not just once, but eternally.

00:12:51.962 --> 00:12:55.139
And when it diverts from what you want,

00:12:55.163 --> 00:12:58.324
we prioritize risk,
we evaluate not just the new stuff,

00:12:58.348 --> 00:12:59.507
but the old stuff.

00:12:59.531 --> 00:13:01.401
We fix it; but most importantly,